  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "c:2858716091",
      "kind": "correctness",
      "harm": "Interrupted in-place writes could corrupt data files without atomic updates or checksum detection",
      "quote": "How worried are we about file corruption here? I thought the main reason we use leveldb and sqlite databases in places like this where we don't need indexing is that they support atomic updates, so you can pull the power cord any time and next time you reboot you will will see some consistent view of the data",
