        "c:2957923761"
      ],
      "fix_pushed": true,
      "settled_by_id": "c:2957923761",
      "settled_by_quote": "The latest push updates the block tree store to use a write ahead log for atomic writes, and crc32c checksums to detect data corruption."
    },
    {
      "id": "rc:3515739871",
      "kind": "correctness",
      "harm": "Directory committing is a no-op on Windows, potentially breaking flag file atomicity and leading to inconsistencies on power loss",
      "quote": "This is a no-op on Windows. I think this can lead to several edge case issues, like the block tree being marked as unpruned when blocks have already been removed, or the WAL not being applied atomically.",
